# Scenario: Wanda, the {{ s.lab.company }} support agent

**{{ s.lab.company }}** is a fictional online vacation-rental marketplace that connects travelers with property hosts around the world. Its guest-support team built **Wanda**, an AI agent that answers booking questions and handles cancellations.

## How Wanda works today

- Wanda is a Python app built with the **OpenAI Agents SDK**. It runs on an engineer's laptop and in a container.
- It calls a model provider directly, with one API key shared by the whole team.
- Its tools read a **CSV snapshot** of bookings, guests, properties and payments that the data team exported by hand ({{ f.snapshot_bookings }} bookings that check in during July 2025).
- It applies the refund policy below, and it can issue a refund on its own.
- Nothing is traced. Quality is checked by reading a few conversations.

## The refund policy

The lab treats **{{ f.today }}** as "today", because the sample data ends in July 2025.

| Cancelled | Refund |
|---|---|
| 14 or more days before check-in | Full refund |
| 7 to 13 days before check-in | 50% refund |
| Less than 7 days before check-in | No refund |

Only bookings with a completed payment can be refunded. Refunds go to the original payment method. The policy says nothing about timelines, fees, vouchers or compensation.

